{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 AB ReaLayer - Multilayer Random Variation Sampler for REAPER. Designed for game audio and sound design workflows.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 AB ReaLayer\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Turn recordings into variations.} A multilayer random variation sampler for REAPER, designed for game audio and sound design.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\pict\pngblip\picw1550\pich1000\picwgoal31000\pichgoal20000 }\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Four drag-and-drop WAV layers with automatic region detection.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Independent volume, pan, pitch, reverse chance and envelopes.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Randomise All, Reset Values and limiter-protected Chaos mode.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab MIDI triggering or one-click Play Sampler.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Editable regions and external WAV recall.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Install through ReaPack\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Import this repository URL in {\b Extensions \u8594 ? ReaPack \u8594 ? Import repositories}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RoadToOmega/AB-ReaLayer/main/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Only the JSFX is installed; no companion script, Python or Ruby is needed to use it. Source WAVs are not bundled.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Existing installations and the 0.11.3 filename change\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Version 0.11.3 uses {\f1 AB_ReaSampler.jsfx} and appears as a new package identity in ReaPack. Synchronize the repository, then select this filename in Browse packages and install it for new instances. Keep the old installed file if saved projects reference it. If ReaPack offers to uninstall an obsolete package, retain it until those projects have been migrated. ReaPack installs into its own repository/category directory and does not automatically migrate those project references. Use the ReaPack-managed copy for new instances. Keep the repository name and Instruments/AB_ReaSampler.jsfx path stable after publication.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Requirements and limits\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A 64-bit REAPER installation with enough free memory is recommended. Each instance preallocates about 770 MiB plus host overhead. Each layer accepts up to 96 MiB of decoded PCM, approximately 65.5 seconds of 96 kHz stereo audio. The limiter adds approximately 2 ms of fixed delay, including when OFF. It limits sample peaks, not true peaks. WAV files remain external.\par}
